A rule of thumb for assessing the cost of operations is to consider the Big O notation, which describes the computational complexity of an algorithm. For example, a simple string scan might be O(n), where n is the length of the string, while a regex evaluation could be O(n*m), where m is the complexity of the regex pattern.

