To avoid waiting too long and risking complications, it's essential to monitor your symptoms closely and seek medical attention if you notice any worsening of the pain, development of fever, chills, vomiting, or any other concerning symptoms. Given your explicit desire for objectivity and the potential seriousness of appendicitis, consulting with a healthcare professional as soon as possible is advisable. They can perform a physical examination, take a detailed medical history, and possibly order diagnostic tests (like imaging studies) to determine the cause of your symptoms and guide appropriate treatment.

