If it turns out to be something like gas instead, you would likely be provided with guidance on managing your symptoms, possibly including dietary advice, over-the-counter medications for symptom relief, and follow-up care if necessary. You wouldn't necessarily be sent home without any follow-up; the healthcare provider might schedule a follow-up appointment to check on your condition, especially if the diagnosis is uncertain or if your symptoms persist or worsen.

