- **Communicate**: If possible, discuss your career development goals with your current employer. They might offer support, such as flexible working hours or additional training opportunities, that can aid your transition.
- **Boundary Setting**: Clearly define your work and personal development time to avoid conflict and maintain productivity in both areas.
- **Review and Adjust**: Regularly assess your progress against your milestones and adjust your strategy as needed. This might involve reallocating time, seeking additional resources, or even reconsidering your transition timeline based on your progress and changing circumstances.

By combining these strategies, you can effectively manage the risks associated with your current role while making steady progress towards your career pivot goals. Remember, flexibility and the ability to adapt your plan as you gather more information and experience will be key to your success.

